ks about cleaning up mixer assignments, routing audio through a mixer, or which group a sound belongs in.\n- unity:build-gtk: Builds node-based Editor tools with Unity Graph Toolkit (GTK) on Unity 6.6+: graphs, nodes, ports and validation, State Machine API tools on 6.7+, and runtime assets via a scripted importer. Use for custom graph, node or state machine editors, or migrating a GraphView tool. Not for Shader Graph, VFX Graph or Animator Controllers.\n- unity:build-live-game: Builds and operates a live game's backend with Unity Gaming Services. Make sure to use this skill when the user wants trusted server-side game logic, player progress, remote configuration, sign-in, achievements, battle passes or leaderboards.\n- unity:craft-game-floors: Makes a Unity game look and feel finished: art style, lighting, juice, sound, menus, saves and look scoring. Use when building a new game's first playable version, or when a game looks like programmer art, feels flat or silent, or needs polish.\n- unity:create-2d-physics: Creates and fixes Unity 2D physics in both systems, 2D Physics Core and the legacy Rigidbody 2D system. Use when the user asks about any 2D physics task, even if neither system is named. Not for 3D physics.\n- unity:create-tile-palette-or-rule-tiles: Create a 2D tile palette from sprites or textures, or make tiles change based on their neighbours. Use for tile palettes or self-connecting tiles, even when the user doesn't name them.\n- unity:generate-editor-search-query: Generates Unity Search queries and opens the Search window to find assets or scene objects. Use when the user asks to find, filter, or list assets, GameObjects, components, or references in the Editor, not on disk.\n- unity:implement-in-app-purchases: Implements, configures, and debugs Unity In-App Purchases, including subscriptions, receipt validation, and direct-to-customer payments via Stripe or Coda. Use when asked about real-money purchases or microtransactions, or migrating from native 